---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import CopyBox from '../components/CopyBox.astro';
import Screenshot from '../components/Screenshot.astro';
import installDone from '../assets/screenshots/companion/install-done.png';
import installOffer from '../assets/screenshots/companion/install-offer.png';
import installPlan from '../assets/screenshots/companion/install-plan.png';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { installCommands } from '../data/releases';
import installPrompt from '../data/generated/install-prompt.txt?raw';
---

<MarketingLayout
	title="Install"
	description="Install pohunek with the coding agent you already use, or by hand on Linux x86_64 and macOS on Apple Silicon."
>
	<section class="container">
		<header class="page-hero">
			<span class="eyebrow">Install</span>
			<h1>Install with your agent</h1>
			<p class="lead">
				The easiest route is to let the agent you already use do the setup. Paste the prompt into Claude Code, Codex or
				another agent with shell access on the machine that should host sessions. It asks for approval before it installs
				the login service or any runtime hook.
			</p>
		</header>
	</section>

	<section class="container section">
		<CopyBox title="install prompt" text={installPrompt.trimEnd()} />
		<p class="muted note">Repeat it on every machine that should host sessions. Remote hosts must join the same NetBird network.</p>
	</section>

	<section class="container section" id="companion">
		<div class="section-head">
			<span class="eyebrow">Desktop companion</span>
			<h2>Install from the companion</h2>
			<p class="lead">
				Start the <a class="text-link" href="/surfaces/companion/">desktop companion</a> on a machine without pohunek and
				it opens a setup screen instead of the session list. It names what is missing: the <code>pohunek</code> command,
				the login service, or a running daemon, and offers to fix it after showing the exact command and what it touches.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="grid companion-install">
			<ol class="steps">
				<li>
					<strong>Install the companion.</strong> On macOS <code>brew install zajca/pohunek/pohunek-companion</code>; on
					Linux x86_64 the release archive from
					<a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/pohunekd/pohunek-companion/releases">pohunekd/pohunek-companion</a>.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Press Install.</strong> On Linux it downloads the pohunek release the companion is built against (never
					"latest") over HTTPS and checks its sha256, and its build attestation when <code>gh</code> is signed in. On macOS
					it runs <code>{site.homebrewInstall}</code>.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Review, then Run.</strong> It shows what the installer will write and runs it only after you press Run and
					confirm. A checksum mismatch refuses the install.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Done.</strong> The setup screen gives way to the session list as soon as the daemon answers.
				</li>
			</ol>
			<div class="install-shots">
				<Screenshot image={installOffer} alt="Companion setup screen offering to install pohunek because the pohunek command is missing" caption="pohunek is missing" />
				<Screenshot image={installPlan} alt="Companion setup screen after the release was downloaded and verified, showing the checksum evidence and what the installer will write" caption="Verified, ready to run" density={1} />
				<Screenshot image={installDone} alt="Companion setup screen after the install finished" caption="Installed" density={1} />
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="container section">
		<div class="section-head">
			<span class="eyebrow">Manual</span>
			<h2>Install by hand</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="grid manual">
			<article class="card">
				<h3>Linux x86_64</h3>
				<p>
					Verified download of the daemon archive (glibc; a <code>-musl</code> archive is published too), then the bundled
					installer copies the binaries under <code>~/.local</code> and registers the login service. It needs systemd 255 or
					newer.
				</p>
				<CopyBox title="linux" text={installCommands.pohunekLinux.join('\n')} />
			</article>
			<article class="card">
				<h3>macOS (Apple Silicon)</h3>
				<p>macOS 14 or newer, tested on macOS 15. Install from the tap, then install the login service.</p>
				<CopyBox title="macos" text={installCommands.pohunekMacos.join('\n')} />
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="container section">
		<p>
			The full procedure, including archive verification, the login service, upgrades and runtime packages, is in the
			<a class="text-link" href="/docs/install/">install guide</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
	.steps {
		margin: 0;
		padding-left: 1.3rem;
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		align-content: start;
		color: var(--ink-muted);
	}
	.steps strong {
		color: var(--ink-strong);
	}
	.install-shots {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 18rem), 1fr));
	}
	.manual {
		align-items: start;
	}
	.note {
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}
</style>
